# lane-harness — line endings for shell scripts.
#
# Add this to .gitattributes. Without it, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# .sh with CRLF, and bash then fails with things like:
#     tools/lane.sh: line 95: $'\r': command not found
# which looks like a broken harness rather than a line-ending problem. install.sh appends this.
*.sh text eol=lf
